# nr-relay-twin-data: reduced by the wire audit (t19). Already applied: the suite and its ledger (tests/twin/scenarios/data, tests/ledger/nr-relay-twin-data.json); no Cargo edit is needed.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/tests/twin/normalise.rs (in-crate edit) is NOT applied
Every scenario that opens a phone leg ends with the relay's own log line
    [relay] phone leg closed client=<first 8 hex of a random UUID> code=<n> reason=<text> lived=<n>ms
whose client prefix is random and whose lived is a duration; without a mask twin_harness_self_check, twin_scenarios and twin_crossover fail on the first scenario with a phone. In Normaliser::value, for an event whose "ev" is "log", apply to its "line" string, after the existing masks: (1) client=([0-9a-f]{8})\b -> client=<id:N> (N from the same first-appearance table identifiers uses, key: the 8 characters); (2) lived=\d+ms -> lived=<ms>. Nothing else of a log line is masked.
CONFLICT to settle by the lead: nr-relay-twin-legs.wire asks for a mask of the same two values with the placeholder <client8> and <ms> (and of phone:<8 hex> and loop-p50/p99/max of the 30 s sockets line). Only one set of placeholders may stay; the twin-legs text is the superset and is exact, apply it and drop this one.
Timing the scenarios rely on: data/feedback_across_runtimes sets feedbackOptions.baseDelayMs to 5000 and waits 7000 ms after the switch (the first segment is shorter than 5 s).
